  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186110719,
      "id": "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca",
      "title": "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1f61827e-fd31-509f-a165-d748740e3f5d",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =4x-5 \\\\ 3x-3x & =4x-5-3x \\\\ 0 & =x-5 \\\\ 0+5 & =x-5+5 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3x=4x-5$ has the unique solution $x=5.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x-6 & =-2x-6 \\\\ -3x-6+3x & =-2x-6+3x \\\\ -6 & =x-6 \\\\ -6+6 & =x-6+6 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-3x-6=-2x-6$ has the unique solution $x=0.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+4 & =-3x+1 \\\\ -3x+4+3x & =-3x+1+3x \\\\ 4 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "6802435d-e588-5c13-9ee4-5752c349613f",
